---
import LegalPage from "../components/LegalPage.astro";
import { GITHUB_REPOSITORY_URL } from "../lib/site";

const sections = [
  ["summary", "Summary"],
  ["usage", "Usage data (off until you say yes)"],
  ["local", "Data that stays on your computer"],
  ["providers", "AI providers you connect"],
  ["contact", "Contact us"],
] as const;
---

<LegalPage
  title="Privacy Policy — Leonidas Code"
  description="What Leonidas Code sends, when, and how to turn it off."
  heading="Leonidas Code Privacy Policy"
  lede="Leonidas Code sends nothing about how you use it unless you say yes. This page lists what it sends if you do."
  eyebrow="Leonidas Code / Legal"
  effectiveDate="2026-11-01"
  lastUpdated="2026-11-01"
  sections={sections}
>
  <section id="summary">
    <p class="section-number">01</p>
    <h2>Summary</h2>
    <p>
      Leonidas Code is a fork of T3 Code by T3 Tools, Inc., under the MIT license. A fresh install
      sends no usage data. Your prompts, files, paths and project names are never part of any usage
      event.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="usage">
    <p class="section-number">02</p>
    <h2>Usage data (off until you say yes)</h2>
    <p>
      The app asks once whether to share usage data. Until you answer Yes, nothing is sent. You can
      change your answer at any time in Settings.
    </p>
    <p>
      If you say Yes, the app sends short events with fixed fields: a random install ID, the app
      version, your operating system, and counts or names from a fixed list. Examples are that the
      app opened, which built-in feature you used, which AI provider you connected, how long setup
      took, and that an error or crash happened. If you type a label for yourself, that label is
      sent too. The events go to PostHog, a product analytics service.
    </p>
    <p>
      The background server of the app has its own usage reporting. It is off by default and stays
      off unless the build or the person who runs it turns it on.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="local">
    <p class="section-number">03</p>
    <h2>Data that stays on your computer</h2>
    <p>
      Your chats, projects, settings and memory files are stored on your computer. Leonidas Code
      does not upload them to us.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="providers">
    <p class="section-number">04</p>
    <h2>AI providers you connect</h2>
    <p>
      When you connect a provider such as Anthropic or OpenAI, the app sends your prompts and the
      context you choose to that provider. The provider's own privacy policy applies to that data.
      We do not see it.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="contact">
    <p class="section-number">05</p>
    <h2>Contact us</h2>
    <p>
      To ask a privacy question or to report a problem, open an issue at{" "}
      <a href={GITHUB_REPOSITORY_URL}>{GITHUB_REPOSITORY_URL}</a>.
    </p>
  </section>
</LegalPage>
